check-ui.ps1 window-resize exercises the staged Window Manager under GDB.
It creates both mono and color windows, gives them nonzero local origins,
and checks growth, shrinking and update-disabled resizing. Pending damage
must survive, unchanged interior pixels must not be added to the update
region, and newly exposed strips must be included when updates are enabled.

DrawNew's region and SaveUpdate semantics follow the user's reference:
Y:/Source Code/supermario/base/SuperMarioProj.1994-02-09/Toolbox/WindowMgr/WindowMgr.a,
DrawNew and SizeGuts. Finder uses SizeWindow for folder zooming. Replacing
its pending update region with the entire content region requested painting
over unchanged pixels that DrawNew had not erased.
